# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in every working tree, on every OS.
#
# Without this, Windows checkouts get CRLF (core.autocrlf=true is the Git for
# Windows default) while macOS and Linux get LF. Terraform then reads different
# bytes from the same commit depending on which machine ran it:
#
#   - Heredoc filters in logging_alerts.tf and billing.tf differ by line ending,
#     so google_logging_metric and google_monitoring_alert_policy show a diff
#     whose - and + lines look character-for-character identical.
#   - terraform/billing_function/*.py hash differently, which changes the
#     archive_file output_md5, which renames the source object and forces both
#     Cloud Functions to redeploy.
#
# Applying from Windows writes CRLF, applying from macOS writes LF back, forever.
# This file is what stops that; pinning the CLI and provider versions does not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — never transform these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.heic binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
